WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.541
Your iPhone as

00:00:01.352 --> 00:00:02.189
a second Mac

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:02.732
display

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.755
PocketDisplayJoe turns

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.581
an iPhone into

00:00:05.393 --> 00:00:06.512
an extra monitor

00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:07.314
for a MacBook

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.281
or Mac mini

00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:09.637
over USB or

00:00:09.449 --> 00:00:10.192
Wi-Fi

00:00:10.726 --> 00:00:11.504
It creates a

00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:12.848
virtual display sized

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.343
to the phone

00:00:13.155 --> 00:00:14.263
at sixty frames

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:14.841
per second

00:00:15.042 --> 00:00:16.327
streamed with hardware

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:16.976
HEVC

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:18.093
Touch works as

00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:18.671
a mouse

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.487
It's native Swift

00:00:20.346 --> 00:00:21.524
and SwiftUI

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:22.822
about two thousand

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:23.883
five hundred lines

00:00:23.954 --> 00:00:25.098
with no accounts

00:00:25.204 --> 00:00:26.395
no cloud and

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:27.373
no analytics

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.908
Full story on

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:29.615
the dashboard
